WEBVTT

00:00:03.096 --> 00:00:07.426
These conversations only work if people say what they actually think.

00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:10.666
And in many teams, that doesn’t happen by itself.

00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:19.006
Psychological safety means people believe they won’t be punished or embarrassed for speaking up, asking a question, or admitting a mistake.

00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:22.726
It’s built slowly, and it can be damaged in a second.

00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:26.906
As the leader, you have more influence on it than anyone else in the room.

00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:29.266
So, a few practical things.

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:32.246
Start with low-risk questions and build up.

00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:35.306
Don’t open with “What’s wrong with how we work?”

00:00:35.356 --> 00:00:38.766
Open with “What’s one thing that went well this month?”

00:00:38.816 --> 00:00:42.586
Honesty grows when people have experienced that it’s safe.

00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:45.446
Use silent writing and anonymous options.

00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:50.886
Post-its, collected and read out by you, let people say things they wouldn’t say out loud.

00:00:50.936 --> 00:00:54.826
Online, an anonymous poll or a shared board does the same.

00:00:54.876 --> 00:00:56.726
Watch your own reactions.

00:00:56.776 --> 00:01:03.206
When someone says something critical, especially about you, your face speaks first. Breathe.

00:01:03.256 --> 00:01:07.386
Say “Thank you, tell me more.” Then really listen.

00:01:07.436 --> 00:01:12.086
The way you react to the first critical comment decides whether there will be a second one.

00:01:12.136 --> 00:01:13.986
Notice the silence too.

00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:17.946
If a topic goes quiet, it’s usually not because everyone agrees.

00:01:17.996 --> 00:01:20.586
You can name it gently: “It’s quiet.

00:01:20.636 --> 00:01:22.746
What would someone who disagrees say?”

00:01:22.796 --> 00:01:26.646
That gives people permission to bring in the other side without owning it.

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:28.886
And finally: follow through.

00:01:28.936 --> 00:01:32.326
If people speak up and nothing changes, they will stop.

00:01:32.376 --> 00:01:36.756
Every agreement you capture and act on makes the next conversation more honest.

